 "boundaries": [
  "Two real native processes per row: one pinned generated VexiiRiscv CPU and one pinned PULP apb_gpio target.",
  "Each case is one CPU -> APB register write -> GPIO real interrupt pulse -> host level wire -> real core trap at the program mtvec -> ISR real APB reads/PADOUTCLR write -> mret -> main RAM check.",
  "The host converts the GPIO transition pulse to the level the core requires and drops it after the actual PADOUTCLR delivery; it injects no trap, cause or vector.",
  "The GPIO input is a declared loopback of its real gpio_out output, not a CPU pin.",
  "The program image is fixed per row and case data comes from a preloaded RAM table; this is not the P6 campaign framework (no online genome mutation, coverage feedback, arbitrary program-image replay or cross-case arbitrary harness reuse)."
 ],
